  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Conservation Livelihoods Approaches Around the WA-Peninsular National Park &#x2013; Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &#x201c;Integrated Conservation Livelihoods Approaches around the Western Area Peninsular National Park (Aberdeen) &#x2013; Phase 2&#x201d; builds on the gains made in the Phase 1 piloted project. The Phase II will strengthen the gaps identified in Phase I to enhance more concrete evidence of the conservation livelihood approach and translate the reflections from the After-Action Review. Based on the documented lessons learnt, the Phase 1 project faced challenges in the implementation, especially with regards the maintenance of the planted mangroves propagules, and ineffectiveness in identifying alternative livelihood option for people engaged in environmental conservation practices for their livelihood. However, the project participants were supported with livestock as an alternative source of livelihoods based on their demand during the Phase I of the project implementation. 
The project will continue to enhance environmental conservation efforts in Big Water and Gbanko communities in the Western Area Rural District while promoting environmentally friendly livelihoods activities. The project will promote good environmental livelihood activities that promote agroforestry, agroecology practices and actively monitor the beneficiaries&apos; involvement in conserving their environment.</narrative>
  </description>
